{
  "abstract": "Let $F=\\mathbf Q(\\zeta_5)$. We construct algebraic correspondences from a fixed primitive CM abelian surface to the relative determinant in degree three of every polarized $F$-sixfold with noncompact signatures at both real places. The determinant is supported on a divisor, with no simplicity, discriminant or generality restriction. A degree-two representation of $G_{16}$ supplies an actual four-dimensional finite-cover source. Removing its common-fixed-line components gives the exact positive Hodge volume $72/125$; canonical-extension positivity and rational Hermitian transfer reach every target. The surface companion changes the mixed-source problem: its Galois action couples to two elliptic companions, and an explicit eight-dimensional Hodge structure has no fully twisted realization on their powers. Every CM abelian source realizing its effective weight-two translate must contain a particular primitive CM fourfold. All sixteen CM types of $\\mathbf Q(\\zeta_{20})$ occur through actual Fermat-20 factors, providing the required source enlargement. Aoki's degree-120 theorem supplies ordinary algebraicity on the enlarged CM sources. Derived-group independence and Abdulali's domination criterion then prove ordinary and generalized Hodge conjectures for mixed powers of pairwise nonisogenous simple sixfolds with exact quartic endomorphism fields, including seven previously constructed biquadratic families, with the specified CM sources. The generic self-power ordinary theorem is already divisor generated; the contribution is the actual determinant correspondence, its support, and the mixed source closure. General rational HC remains open.",
